\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Rips vs.\ DTM$_5$ on one clustered cloud (two blobs joined by a sparse two-point bridge), same intermediate filtration value $r$: Rips already merges the blobs through the bridge (left, top), while DTM$_5$ delays exactly that merge because the bridge sits in a sparse neighbourhood (left, bottom) -- shown in the $H_0$ diagrams (right) by the highlighted merge event sitting much further from the diagonal's origin under DTM.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
